<title>INDIA: Coal India revises prices of non-coking coal.</title>
<headline>Coal India revises prices of non-coking coal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Coal Ministry said on Friday that state-run Coal India Ltd (CIL) had raised the prices of certain grades of non-coking, run-of-mine coal with effect from April 1, 1997.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> NON-COKING COAL     REVISED PRICES   EARLIER PRICES</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>  Grade D		     524		  406</p>
<p>  Grade E		     416		  322</p>
<p>  Grade F		     332		  257</p>
<p>  Grade G		     237		  183</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE - Prices are in rupees per tonne. The ministry released the revised prices in a statement. Coal India is the monopoly coal producer in India.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
